# MOBILE PORT NOTE: Node (Mainapi) and this Python server (proxiesembed)
# are two embedded runtimes living inside the SAME single Android process
# (native libnode.so via JNI + Chaquopy's libpython3.11.so both loaded into
# this app's one process). Both load_dotenv()/dotenv.config() calls mutate
# the SAME OS-level process environment table (os.environ / process.env are
# both backed by real getenv/setenv, not per-runtime sandboxes), and neither
# python-dotenv nor Node's dotenv overrides a key that's already set -- so
# whichever runtime's .env loads first wins any shared key name. Node's own
# env.production (android-app/scripts/zip_node_backend.py's bundle) already
# defines PORT=3000, DB_HOST, DB_PORT, DB_USER, DB_PASSWORD, DB_NAME -- do
# NOT redeclare any of those names here even with an empty/unused value, or
# whichever runtime starts first silently wins that key for BOTH. server.py
# hardcodes PORT=25569 itself (never reads it from env), so it doesn't need
# a PORT entry here at all.
PROXY_BASE=
PROXIES_SOCKS5_JSON=
SIBNET_PROXY_SOCKS5_JSON=
FRANCETV_EMAIL=
FRANCETV_PASSWORD=
DEEPBRID_API_KEY=
REAL_DEBRID_API_KEY=
